{
  "_what": "Second-pass human reference labels for the Phase 6C scene-understanding benchmark. Supersedes human_labels.json for scoring; the first pass is kept for provenance.",
  "_why_a_second_pass": "The first pass was transcribed from ONE frame per video (t=1.0s) while the model is shown four hook frames (0,1,2,3s) plus two later context frames. That made 47 disagreements unscoreable: the model said true, the single labelled frame said false, and nothing in the data said which was right. Reviewing the full frame strips resolved them - and showed the first pass had under-called presence in 14 videos where the object was plainly there at t=0 or t=3.",
  "_rule": "A boolean is true if the thing is visible in ANY of the four HOOK frames (t=0,1,2,3). Frames at 5s and 12s are excluded, because server/ai/vision_task.py PROMPT tells the model those are supplied only to judge whether the opening is representative, and scoring the model on them would charge it for following its instructions.",
  "_ordering_disclosure": "This pass was written AFTER inference had been run, which the first pass was not. The question asked of each strip was 'is X visible in frames 0-3', which is a question about the frames; the per-video prediction table was not opened until this file was saved. Three videos (451, 237, 514) had been inspected against predictions before the relabel began, and that is a real, if small, contamination of those three rows.",
  "_labelled_on": "2026-10-26",
  "_definitions": {
    "hands_visible": "Hands visible anywhere in the frame. The schema gives this field no description, so the literal reading is used - id514's hands are at his sides, and that counts.",
    "face_visible": "A human face visible, including a partial face (id421 is a mouth-and-beard close-up) and a face reflected in the piano lid (id453, id456). Not who it is.",
    "text_overlay_present": "Creator-added text only. Sheet-music markings are not an overlay, per prompt rule 5.",
    "setting": "The most defensible of the schema's seven values. Several are genuinely ambiguous on this corpus - see _ambiguity."
  },
  "_ambiguity": "stage vs concert_hall, and studio vs home_room, are not cleanly separable on this material. id243 is a blue-lit hall with an audience (concert_hall here, 'stage' in pass one); id512 is a panelled room that could be either studio or home_room. Disagreements on `setting` should be read as partly a taxonomy problem, not purely model error.",
